---
description: NEAR smart contract rules (Rust, near-sdk)
globs: contracts/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Use `near-sdk` 5.30.x and `near-contract-standards` 5.30.x. Don't hand-roll NEP-171/177/178/181/199.
- Use `#[near(contract_state)]`, `#[near]` impl blocks, `#[private]` for callbacks, and `#[callback_result]` for promise results.
- Require storage deposits for state-growing calls and refund the excess.
- Use explicit access control: owner, minters, attestor relayers. Add a unit test for every privileged method being rejected for other callers.
- Never store or accept an EVM/HL address for a trader.
- Sandbox tests use `near-workspaces`. Build with `cargo near build non-reproducible-wasm`.
- OutLayer: call `request_execution(code_source, resource_limits, input_data, secrets_ref, response_format, payer_account_id)` on the configured `outlayer_id`, and pin `attestor_code_hash` in the callback.
